runtime: quiesce control thread before closing listener

Stop and join the runner's control thread before closing its UNIX listener,
then remove only its own control socket. This avoids intentional listener
closure racing a pending accept while preserving unexpected thread failures
and the engine's strict namespace and exit-proof checks.

Exercise the ordering through the real listener and public stop. Preserve
fixture primary failures, report secondary cleanup failures, and retain
private native diagnostics before temporary fixture removal. State formats
and cleanup permissions are unchanged; retained campaigns gain no recovery
or cleanup authority.
